This is how I set this:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "external_directory": {
      "*": "ask",
      "/tmp/**": "allow"
    }
  }
}
```

You could also try to add another entry like `"{env:TMPDIR}/**": "allow"`, but I wouldn't do it... if that env variable is not set, it could have pretty unpleasant consequences in case it resolves to `"/**"`.

Thanks @pwilkin. Given this is actually coming from the model template (Qwen 3.5) and not the parser:
```
    {%- if message.role == "system" %}
        {%- if not loop.first %}
            {{- raise_exception('System message must be at the beginning.') }}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- elif message.role == "user" %}
```
this should probably best be handled on OpenCode's end.
